CHEMTRAIN-DEPLOY package
========================

The source tree contains the optional in-tree chemtrain-deploy package. The
package provides ``pair_style chemtrain``, ``pair_style chemtrain/kk``, and
matching computes for exported particle and configuration outputs.

Build `libconnector.so` before configuring LAMMPS:

  cmake -S cmake -B build-chemtrain \
    -D PKG_CHEMTRAIN-DEPLOY=ON \
    -D CHEMTRAIN_DEPLOY_ROOT=/path/to/chemtrain/chemtrain-deploy \
    -D CHEMTRAIN_DEPLOY_LIBCONNECTOR=/path/to/libconnector.so \
    -D BUILD_MPI=ON

Enable the LAMMPS Kokkos package and the appropriate CUDA architecture to build
``chemtrain/kk``.

The connector is an external shared library and must be built with a compatible
compiler, MPI implementation, and accelerator runtime. Its directory must be
discoverable by the dynamic loader when LAMMPS starts, for example through
``LD_LIBRARY_PATH`` on Linux. LAMMPS neither distributes nor builds the
connector.

The package was contributed by Paul Fuchs (paul.fuchs@tum.de).

Additional documentation is at https://chemtrain.readthedocs.io/.

The LAMMPS package is compiled into the executable. The ``plugin load`` command
and ``LAMMPS_PLUGIN_PATH`` do not load the package.
